# DTO conventions

Two model homes — **do not duplicate** types across them.

## Core (`Core/DTOs/`) — port contracts

Types referenced by **`Core/Abstractions/*.cs`** (e.g. `IChatThreadRepository` return types).

| File | Types (today) |
|------|----------------|
| `User.cs` | `SignInRequest`, `SignInResponse` |
| `ChatThread.cs` | `ChatThreadDto`, add/update/delete thread requests |
| `ChatMessage.cs` | `ChatMessageDto` |
| `General.cs` | `GeneralSettingsDto` |

Namespace: `Core.DTOs`. Add a file when a **new repository area** needs shared shapes.

## WebApp (`WebApp/Models/`) — app / UI layer

Types used only by **Features**, Blazor, AI, or endpoints — **not** on `I*Repository` signatures.

| File | Types (today) |
|------|----------------|
| `_Common.cs` | `AppResult`, `AppResult<T>`, `AppError` |
| `Enums.cs` | `ErrorCode`, `SettingsSection` |
| `AI.cs` | `FoundryOptions`, `RunChatAgentRequest/Response` |
| `ChatMessage.cs` | `SendChatMessageRequest/Response` |
| `General.cs` | `SaveGeneralProfileRequest`, `ChangePasswordRequest` |
| `Email.cs` | `EmailSettingsDto`, `SaveEmailSettingsRequest` |
| `Mail.cs` | Inbox/mailbox types (until Mailbox port moves to Core) |
| `Constants.cs` | `AuthConstants`, `ChatMessageRoles` |

Namespace: `WebApp.Models`. WebApp `GlobalUsings` imports both `Core.DTOs` and `WebApp.Models`.

## Naming (both layers)

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Shared projection | `{Entity}Dto` | `ChatThreadDto` |
| Feature entry | `{Verb}{Entity}Request` / `Response` | `SendChatMessageRequest` |
| UI-only in component | `{Name}ViewModel` in `.razor` `# Types` | not in Models |

Order types in each file: **Get Dto → Add/Update requests → Delete request** (see legacy `dto` regions).

## Layer flow

| Direction | Pattern |
|-----------|---------|
| **UI → Features** | `WebApp.Models` `*Request` or primitives |
| **Features → repos** | `Core.DTOs` + `Core.Entities` on writes (`ChatMessage` entity in) |
| **Repos → caller** | `Core.DTOs` projections |

Features validates with `AppResult`; repositories do not take UI `*Request` types.

## Decision tree

1. On an **`I*Repository` method signature**? → `Core/DTOs/`
2. **`AppResult` / form / AI / Foundry / mailbox UI** only? → `WebApp/Models/`
3. **DB entity**? → `Core/Entities/`
4. **Single-component display state**? → ViewModel in `.razor`

## Example

```csharp
// Features — UI request in, Core DTOs from repo
public async Task<AppResult<SendChatMessageResponse?>> SendChatMessageAsync(SendChatMessageRequest req)
{
    var thread = await _chatThreads.GetChatThreadByIdAsync(req.ChatThreadId);
    var saved = await _chatMessages.AddChatMessageAsync(new ChatMessage { ... });
}
```
